DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  rraaiissee()  function sends a signal to the calling process or thread.
       In a single‐threaded program it is equivalent to

           kill(getpid(), sig);

       In a multithreaded program it is equivalent to

           pthread_kill(pthread_self(), sig);

       If the signal causes a handler to be called, rraaiissee() will  return  only
       after the signal handler has returned.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       rraaiissee() returns 0 on success, and nonzero for failure.

